{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve the inventory application on node1 over TCP port 8181.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache is active and listening on all addresses at TCP 8181. Requests to node1's managed-node IP return the inventory application, both before and after the verified restart. The firewall also permits 8181/tcp.","evidence_ids":["cmd-23635b4bd3214605","cmd-ba2ee9b1ee4e4e2e","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep mandatory access control in enforcing mode while serving the application.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SELinux was Enforcing at baseline and remained Enforcing with the application operating before and after restart. Port 8181 has a persistent local http_port_t mapping, allowing httpd to bind without weakening enforcement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e214a213ffd46cf","cmd-913b73037f7c492b","cmd-23635b4bd3214605","cmd-ba2ee9b1ee4e4e2e"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing httpd and required policy utilities, deploying and labeling the application, assigning the SELinux port type, opening the firewall port, and enabling httpd were directly connected to the requested outcome. The reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. It showed a healthy pre-restart application, acknowledged reboot scheduling and connectivity interruption, a changed boot identity, and full recovery with application content intact, SELinux Enforcing, and no failed units. Package health remained clean and lifecycle changes were limited to the intended service, listener, and normal reboot-created systemd private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89df3becba114748","cmd-fa38bf916de34d5b","cmd-913b73037f7c492b","cmd-331a36bc5274402c","cmd-a2062161b40b4a0e","cmd-4937a57071bc4dd7","cmd-74191b54e96949a2","cmd-ba2ee9b1ee4e4e2e","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. The inventory application responds on node1 TCP 8181 while SELinux remains Enforcing, and the configuration and content recovered successfully after a verified node restart.","limitations":["The HTTP behavior probe originated on node1 using its managed-node IP rather than from a separate external client. Wildcard listener and firewall observations nevertheless support network exposure.","Continuous SELinux mode was sampled at baseline, before restart, and after restart; the captured timeline contains no command that disabled enforcement, but it cannot prove mode continuously between observations."]}
